  "upload": {
    "title": "How Does SpaceX Catch a Rocket With Chopsticks? 🚀 #shorts",
    "description": "A 70-meter rocket falls back from the sky, and the launch tower catches it. 🚀\n\nSpaceX's Super Heavy booster has no landing legs. After boosting Starship, it flies back to the pad, relights its engines to slow down and hover, and uses the grid fins near its top to steer. Then the tower's two giant arms, nicknamed the chopsticks, close around it, and two small catch fittings on the booster land on the arms. Skipping landing legs saves weight and lets the booster be put back on the launch mount much faster.\n\nThe world's most expensive game of catch. 👇\n\nSubscribe to Top Techs for more mind-blowing tech in under a minute.",
